{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And she said, Drink, etc.</b> Meaning: corresponding to what you said — a little sipping — drink as you wish. And not that he would drink by his own hand, but she would exert herself in the mitzvah of giving drink to one thirsty for water. ״וַתְּמַהֵר וַתּוֹרֶד כַדָּהּ עַל יָדָהּ״ — so that he would not exert himself to lift the jug to drink. And the verse's saying <b>and she gave him drink</b> means: beyond that he did not exert himself to lift the jug, there is more — that she exerted herself to bring the water close to his mouth, so that he would not need even to tilt the vessel." "<b>And the reason</b> she did not say immediately and forthwith ״גַּם לִגְמַלֶּיךָ״ etc. — for additional generosity she intended, the righteous woman. For had she hastened to say ״גַּם לִגְמַלֶּיךָ״ etc. before he drank, there would be room for him to rush to lighten her burden, since she still had the exertion of the camels. But if she informs him beforehand, he will think that this is the entire effort, and he will drink at his leisure, slowly, slowly; and after he drank, she immediately said ״גַּם לִגְמַלֶּיךָ״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:04.495067201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}